 "statement": "LocalizedFamilyData contains the original five data fields hShift, hLocalization, scalarLocalization, gamma and a. Name each of the original nineteen quantified law propositions transparently. LocalizedFamilyLaws records exactly those nineteen laws. LocalizedFamily contains this data and all of these laws; its original named data and proof accessors have the original parameter and result types. This is the fieldwise-equivalent representation of the normalized localized family used in the rational purity endpoint theorem. No normalization, canonical comparison, counit mate, or coherence condition is dropped.",
